Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:39:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06861/11362] [outer-loop] ARC r11l round-4: L4->L5, selection
 occlusion was the wall

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on r11l solved L5, directly answering
round-3's "revisit delivery order" recommendation with a different root
cause: SELECTION OCCLUSION. After cargo attaches to a handle, clicking an
overlapped handle center doesn't select it -- it moves the currently
selected handle instead. Moving the visible selected handle away first
exposes the buried handle, allowing all carrier handles to route
independently. Cargo pairs by complementary masks (8+9 at left-center,
b+e at upper-right; three other dotted glyphs are decoys); with correct
ordering both carriers fuse and deliver within the 60-click meter.

Fresh-reset reproduce() gate passed (reached_level=5). Independently
re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=5, state=NOT_FINISHED.

reproducible_total_levels 147 -> 148. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
